@900 = ~I met Dar'kan, a warehouse worker transformed into a thinking werewolf by an enchanted rune. He suggested asking Thalantyr at High Hedge for help.~
@901 = ~Thalantyr suspects a magical Symbol and must examine Dar'kan in person. I should return to the River District warehouse and escort him.~
@902 = ~Dar'kan is at High Hedge. Thalantyr has discovered an arcane binding, and needs a moonstone to prepare a counter-enchantment.~
@903 = ~The counter-enchantment manifested a spectral wolf! We must destroy it before Dar'kan can recover.~
@904 = ~Dar'kan is restored to his elven form. The arcane wolf is defeated, and Thalantyr's counter-enchantment succeeded.~
@905 = ~Warehouses are not for quests. You are not authorised to be here, so leave.~
@906 = ~Who are you to tell me to leave? Are you authorised?!~
@907 = ~I go where I wish. If you have a problem with that, deal with it.~
@908 = ~I am leaving. Fine.~
@909 = ~I told you to leave this warehouse. Do not make me repeat myself.~
@910 = ~Fine. I'll go.~
@911 = ~I won't take orders from you.~
@912 = ~You asked for trouble. Now you're going to get it!~
@913 = ~I have full authority! Black! Evie! Get them!~
@914 = ~You just spoke your last. Black! Evie! Attack!~
@915 = ~Best decision you've ever made.~
@916 = ~I hate this job. Lift this, lift that, put it there, hold that. Argh, my back's in pain.~
@917 = ~Halt! Do not venture further into the warehouse. Not when Dar'kan is there.~
@918 = ~Who?~
@919 = ~Dar'kan is one of our fellow workers. He recently fell victim to some vile curse. He's not entirely... himself at the moment, so I'd advise you to leave. For your own good.~
@920 = ~Have you spoken to Thalantyr?~
@921 = ~Yes. He needs to examine you in person. Get ready for a long journey; we must take you to him.~
@922 = ~I'm about to.~
@923 = ~You're back? Changed your mind, or come back to gawk in curiosity?~
@924 = ~We'll try to find a wizard or a priest who could help you.~
@925 = ~Any ideas where I could seek help?~
@926 = ~No. I cannot help you.~
@927 = ~Please, find Thalantyr at High Hedge. I'm afraid to leave this place in my present form.~
@928 = ~Who goes there? Daltan, is that you?~
@929 = ~No. I am an adventurer. I mean you no harm, as long as you don't attack me.~
@930 = ~Werewolf, huh?~
@931 = ~Die, beast!~
@932 = ~I hope Thalantyr knows what he's doing.~
@933 = ~No, wait! Please!~
@934 = ~Have no fear. I am not going to attack you. I've been afflicted with lycanthropy for a few days now.~
@935 = ~A few days? And you're capable of retaining intelligence and free will in this form?~
@936 = ~Is that... unusual? I know nothing about lycanthropy save for its name. I shouldn't have touched that damned merchandise.~
@937 = ~How did you come into contact with it?~
@938 = ~Cernd, I may need your insight. Why would a freshly turned werewolf be sentient immediately after transformation?~
@939 = ~I am responsible for loading boxes with varied types of merchandise from across the seas. Been doing that for years and among all trinkets and rubbish I've touched, never have I ever become a dupe to a curse. Blasted magic!~
@940 = ~The object... it resembled a glowing star symbol on a dark obsidian stone. A rune of sorts, I believe. Some words in an ancient language were engraved on the back, but I couldn't read it. My elven heritage seems not to pay off much.~
@941 = ~I threw it into the river, hoping the distance could reverse the spell. I should've sought help at a local temple or found a mage, but... I can't revert back to my elven self. I lost track of the days; it's been a while since I became this... beast. Guards would slaughter me if they saw me wandering the streets.~
@942 = ~So, you cannot switch forms at will, nor do you have animalistic instincts taking over, and you can communicate verbally. That's a hybrid I've never seen.~
@943 = ~Any idea where that merchandise is from?~
@944 = ~I don't know for certain. It was part of the merchandise sent here from across the seas. I certainly won't be handling any more such cargo!~
@945 = ~I should be glad about the 'no-aggressor' part. I'd be damned if I sunk my teeth into my fellow workers or anyone else. Will you help me? I don't know what to do.~
@946 = ~Please.~
@947 = ~We'll try to find a wizard or a priest who could help you.~
@948 = ~Any ideas where I could seek help?~
@949 = ~I am not familiar with curses, nor do I have time to ask every wizard I meet. I'm sorry. Ask someone else.~
@950 = ~I may have a suggestion. North of Amn, a small town called Beregost hosts a lonely mage living in seclusion, west of it. His name is Thalantyr. I'd try there if you're up for a longer trip. I really hope you can help me. I pray for it.~
@951 = ~Guess I shall spend more time locked away in this rat-infested warehouse. Great. May fate send me some actual adventurers for a change—no pun intended.~
@952 = ~I can already see stares from all passers-by. All right. I am ready.~
@953 = ~Yes, Master Thalantyr. My name is Dar'kan, and as you can see, I'm suffering from an odd case of lycanthropy. I'm growing desperate with each day.~
@954 = ~Now that you mention it... yes! Something on my chest, beneath all this fur. I thought it was a scar from transforming. Why?~
@955 = ~What?! But... look at me! I'm a werewolf!~
@956 = ~Wonderful. I've become someone else's magical mistake.~
@957 = ~So someone invented a spell to help werewolves stay sane, but forgot the part where they turn back into normal people?~
@958 = ~Can you undo it, Master Thalantyr?~
@959 = ~Couldn't agree more. I've had enough of hiding from people who would sooner put a sword through me than ask my name.~
@960 = ~That's... hardly reassuring.~
@961 = ~Competence. Definitely competence.~
@962 = ~I don't suppose this will hurt?~
@963 = ~Agh! Something's happening! I can feel it beneath my skin!~
@964 = ~I... I can't! It's pulling me apart!~
@965 = ~My... my hands! They're back! And my face... I can feel my face again!~
@966 = ~I can't believe it. I'm myself again! Master Thalantyr, you've saved my life!~
@967 = ~I cannot thank you enough. I thought I'd spend the rest of my life as some wretched beast. I don't have much gold, but please, take what I've saved. You've earned it.~
@968 = ~Truly? That's remarkably generous of you. I won't forget this kindness. Should you find yourself in Athkatla again, seek me out. Perhaps I can return the favour someday.~
@969 = ~Of course. It isn't much, but it's the least I can offer. You've spared me a life of misery, and for that I'll be forever grateful.~
@970 = ~Hah! You have my word. In fact, I might reconsider my occupation altogether. Something involving less magic and considerably fewer crates sounds appealing!~
@971 = ~I'd best return to Athkatla. Daltan must wonder where I've disappeared to. Imagine his face when I tell him what happened!~
@972 = ~Fair enough. Farewell, and may fortune favour you all!~
@973 = ~We came here on behalf of an elf from Athkatla. He has been marked by a lycanthropy curse that caused a sudden transformation into a werewolf. He retains his intelligence and clarity of mind, has not given in to feral instincts, and has not turned back into his elven form at all. He touched a magically imbued rune that activated the curse, but then threw the rune into the river. Can you help him?~
@974 = ~Given that the object is no more, I can't analyse it thoroughly to see what it was. I would need to see the object first; however, your description aligns with one theory. High-level spellcasters can cast a spell called Symbol, painting a magical rune on a wall, a door, or even a piece of rock. If you look at it or touch it, it triggers instantly.~
@975 = ~Sometimes glyphs or symbols attune to the recipient through their tangled magic, and eliminating the object responsible is not enough to erase its effects. Does the sufferer have the symbol from the rune anywhere on his body?~
@976 = ~We don't know. He hasn't told us.~
@977 = ~I might need to see him, then. I am aware this is a long journey back, but if I am to lift this curse, I need to study him. His lack of the major werewolf transformation symptoms, such as bloodthirst and bestial impulses, is unheard of. I cannot risk preparing a natural concoction for him without understanding his condition.~
@978 = ~Inform him to come to me at once if he wishes to be rid of it. A curse triggered by an unknown rune could prove grave and lead to even more undesired side effects.~
@979 = ~So, you're the one afflicted with the curse, I'd wager?~
@980 = ~Let me look at you. Remain still. Hmm. Curious indeed. Tell me, Dar'kan, have you noticed any unusual markings since the transformation? A scar, perhaps, like the symbol you described?~
@981 = ~Because I can sense an arcane imprint beneath your skin. The enchantment has not merely altered your appearance. It has bound itself to your very essence. And you are not suffering from ordinary lycanthropy. Indeed, I doubt you've contracted lycanthropy at all.~
@982 = ~You possess the physical characteristics of a werewolf, certainly. But appearances deceive, especially when magic is concerned.~
@983 = ~Now, what would you like to know?~
@984 = ~Are you saying the rune transformed him without actually infecting him?~
@985 = ~What magic could cause such an unusual transformation?~
@986 = ~More importantly, can you reverse it?~
@987 = ~Precisely. The enchantment imitates lycanthropy without the underlying disease. That explains his retained intelligence and lack of uncontrollable aggression. His mind remains his own.~
@988 = ~An ancient transmutation combined with powerful binding magic. Such experiments attempted to separate lycanthropes' physical form from their bestial instincts. Some were merciful; others were quite the opposite.~
@989 = ~Possibly, but I must understand the enchantment before attempting to dispel it, or the man might be permanently disfigured or worse.~
@990 = ~The symbol upon his chest appears to be the key. I suspect the original spell tried to preserve a lycanthrope's consciousness while binding the subject permanently to his transformed state.~
@991 = ~An oversimplification, but not entirely inaccurate. The experiment may have failed, its magic lying dormant until Dar'kan touched the stone. Without the original rune, I must devise a counter-enchantment.~
@992 = ~The lost rune makes this harder than it needed to be. But I shall prepare an alternative. The enchantment has left its signature in your skin.~
@993 = ~With the proper materials, yes. I require a moonstone of sufficient quality to draw the lunar transformation from his body. My remaining ingredients are already at hand.~
@994 = ~We have a moonstone. Will this suffice?~
@995 = ~Where can we obtain a moonstone?~
@996 = ~Are you certain this procedure will work?~
@997 = ~An acceptable specimen. Then there is no reason to delay. Dar'kan, step forward.~
@998 = ~Any competent jeweller should be able to provide one. Return with a moonstone. Until then, our afflicted friend should remain here in safety.~
@999 = ~There are no certainties when undoing ancient magic. I am confident I can separate the spell from him, but I cannot promise it will surrender peacefully.~
@1000 = ~Would you prefer reassurance or competence?~
@1001 = ~Have you found a moonstone? The afflicted elf cannot remain in that form indefinitely.~
@1002 = ~Yes. I have one here.~
@1003 = ~Not yet.~
@1004 = ~Stand in the circle, Dar'kan, and do not move until I instruct you otherwise.~
@1005 = ~I wouldn't count on it being pleasant. I shall begin the counter-enchantment.~
@1006 = ~The binding is weakening. Hold still!~
@1007 = ~By Mystra, the enchantment is resisting! Stand back! An arcane manifestation is forming, a guardian of the curse. Destroy it before it reattaches itself to him!~
@1008 = ~There. The enchantment has been severed. Now, let us finish what we started.~
@1009 = ~Yes, yes, I can see your hands. Now, unless you intend to spend the entire day examining them, perhaps you could step out of my circle?~
@1010 = ~Your gratitude is acknowledged. Though you have these adventurers to thank more than me. Without their intervention you would still be hiding in that warehouse.~
@1011 = ~And what do you say, adventurers?~
@1012 = ~We're glad we could help. Keep your gold.~
@1013 = ~Thank you. We could use the reward.~
@1014 = ~Just promise you'll stop touching suspicious magical objects.~
@1015 = ~If you are done, Dar'kan, I suggest returning to your affairs. I will not be putting you through that procedure again.~
@1016 = ~I'd advise keeping the details to yourself. Such stories have a habit of attracting the wrong sort of attention.~
@1017 = ~As if elven heritage ever pays off.~
@1018 = ~We must restore him to his former self. He needs us.~
@1019 = ~I'm more concerned with the fact that he retains his ability to speak and communicate clearly, and his animalistic cravings haven't taken over. Tell me, are you experiencing any hard-to-contain sensations and hunger right now? Is your mind fixated on food?~
@1020 = ~N-not really... I do seem to be more into meat right now. I consumed a few raw chickens from nearby mere days ago, but that quickly satisfied my hunger. W-why? Is that abnormal?~
@1021 = ~Lycanthropy replaces your sane instincts with animalistic fury. Commonly, the afflicted person loses themselves to the transformation and recovers little to no memories from when they switch forms. Your case is particularly uncommon, as you bypassed these rules. Can you tell me, what was that merchandise you came into contact with?~
@1022 = ~I threw it away. Straight into the river. I thought maybe the distance could bring my human shape back. It didn't work, though, and I've been stuck in this form for days.~
@1023 = ~Are you saying you haven't changed back into your original form even once?~
@1024 = ~No. Touching the object transformed me immediately, and I've been like this ever since.~
@1025 = ~And the object? What was it? What did it look like?~
@1026 = ~It resembled a glowing star symbol on a dark obsidian stone. A rune of sorts, I believe. Some words in an ancient language were engraved on the back, but I couldn't read it. My elven heritage seems not to pay off much.~
@1027 = ~As if elven heritage ever pays off.~
@1028 = ~Mystic rune and ancient language... I am not familiar with runes, nor could I decipher their meaning. Since we have lost the object, the best course of action is to find someone who knows about curses awakened by ancient magic.~
@1029 = ~It seems this unusual ordeal has taught us all something about ancient magic.~
@1030 = ~The unnatural bond has been severed and balance restored. Even harmless-looking trinkets can hide powers beyond our understanding.~
@1031 = ~A wise decision. Perhaps there is hope for your intelligence after all.~
@1032 = ~I'm killing the next werewolf we meet. I don't care what you say, <CHARNAME>.~
@1033 = ~I cannot thank you enough. I thought I would spend the rest of my life as a beast. I have a little gold saved, if you'll take it. You have earned it.~
